.Dd November 5, 2026
.Dt RM 1
.Os ABSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm rm
.Nd remove files or directory trees
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl r
.Ar path ...
.Nm
.Fl f
.Op Fl r
.Op Ar path ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Remove each file, or with
.Fl r ,
a directory and its descendants.
Without
.Fl r ,
directory operands are refused.
With
.Fl f ,
missing paths are ignored and no operands is successful.
Other errors and the refusals below are still reported.
Without
.Fl f ,
missing paths are errors.
There is no interactive confirmation.
The short flags may be combined as
.Fl rf
or
.Fl fr .
Options precede operands; a later option word is a path.
.Ql --
ends option processing; use it or a
.Ql ./
prefix for a name beginning with a dash.
Unknown leading options return status 2.
.Pp
Final path components
.Ql .
and
.Ql ..
are refused.
A session mount point is refused before removal.
For recursive removal, a directory containing a session mount is also
refused before traversal; inability to establish this condition is a
refusal, not permission to proceed.
.Pp
Only this process's writable filesystem view is usable.
Success is silent; failures go to standard error and later operands are
attempted.
Recursive removal may partially succeed; there is no transaction or undo
for the entire tree.
See
.Xr sync 1
for durability of accepted changes.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when all removals succeeded or missing paths were ignored with
.Fl f ;
1 for another failed or refused path;
2 for missing operands without
.Fl f
or an unknown leading option.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
rm /home/operator/notes/old
rm -r /home/operator/notes-copy
rm -rf /home/operator/temporary-tree
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mkdir 1 ,
.Xr sync 1 ,
.Xr filesystem 7
